# Project Root vs AI Coding Separation

Purpose:
  Keep human code and AI execution context separate.

Structure:
  project/                 # Human code root
    backend/
    frontend/
    database/
    tests/
    docs/                  # Human-readable docs
      index.md

  .sdd/                     # AI context root
    PROJECT.sdd             # Project intent
    project/                # AI project model
      PROJECT.sdd
      docs/                 # Human docs mirror
      sdd/                  # AI executable model
      tasks/
      decisions/
      gates/
    chains/                 # Execution chains
      graph.sdd
      default.sdd
      arms/
      rules/
      tokens/
    skills/                 # Skill catalog
    prompts/                # Prompt templates
    workflows/              # Workflow definitions
    state/                  # State notation

Rules:
  [S1] AI MUST start from .sdd/, never from project/ directly.
  [S2] AI MUST read .sdd/project/docs/ before touching project/.
  [S3] AI MUST get human approval before writing to project/.
  [S4] project/ is the source of truth for code.
  [S5] .sdd/ is the source of truth for intent.
  [S6] docs/ under project/ is human language.
  [S7] .sdd/project/sdd/ is AI language.

Context Flow:
  prompt
    -> .sdd/chains/arms/prompt.sdd (P1)
    -> .sdd/project/docs/ (human docs)
    -> human approval
    -> .sdd/project/sdd/ (AI model)
    -> .sdd/chains/arms/code.sdd (C1)
     -> project/ (human code)

State: +
